laude"},{"repo_name":"ryzom/ryzomcore","commit_timestamp":"2026-07-07T10:48:01Z","branch":"core4","commit_sha":"a53fedd18f81167d95cb88b9bac9ad57501e5d8c","github_link":"https://github.com/ryzom/ryzomcore/commit/a53fedd18f81167d95cb88b9bac9ad57501e5d8c","commit_subject":"Pipeline_max_export_shape: texture-matrix (animated-material) export — waterfalls scroll, byte-exact. The shape process writes a per-node <node>.anim (NelExportAnimation) for nodes with AUTOMATIC_ANIMATION; for the animated-material class (scrolling-water) that is the texture-matrix tracks (addMtlTracks/addTexTracks). New anim_build: walk the node's material tree (typed CMtlBase/CMultiMtl), for each material with bExportTextureMatrix resolve its texmap's StdUVGen U/V Offset Linear Float controller (§10k) and emit a CTrackKeyFramerLinearFloat named <mtl>.UTrans<stage>/.VTrans<stage>; a Multi resolves its own track through its first sub-material and recurses (subs first, matching the reference insertion order that CAnimation preserves as the track-data index). Crux: bExportTextureMatrix / bEnableSlot are often NOT constants — the artist keyed the export flag with an On/Off controller (0x984b8d27) — so shared resolveNelBoolAt0 (scene_lib) evaluates the controller at tick 0, and material_build uses it too so enableUserTexMat fires (otherwise the material carries no user texture matrix for the anim to drive — the \"not moving in-game\" class). Exporter gains --anim-out; shape_corpus.py gates the produced .anim byte-exact against ~/core4_data/*_shapes references. Gate: full shape corpus T1/T2 2850/2850, T3 unchanged (767 float-eq + 320 diff), material anim 67/67 byte-identical.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"MervinPraison/PraisonAI","commit_timestamp":"2026-07-07T10:47:46Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"cbdebd1de612debd2ba4fd76e84d3a9288e935d4","github_link":"https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI/commit/cbdebd1de612debd2ba4fd76e84d3a9288e935d4","commit_subject":"Merge pull request #2703 from Mervi